    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Crīsa</span></b> , ae, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρῖσα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient town of Phocis, on the
			sea</i>, now <i>Crisso</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 3, 4,
				§ 8</span></i>.—Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Crīsaeus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>of Crisa</i>: sinus = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλπος Κρισαῖος</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 3, 4,
				§ 7</span></i>.</div>
